THE PROBLEM
Trying to run newly installed WordPress from the Apache2 server; kept getting 404 Error Not Found 

TROUBLESHOOTING
I checked that my file physically exisited and running and permissions were entered correctly
I used the command ls -l /var/www/html/wordpress/ confirming that the file was present
I went back through the Burns 6.1 Wordress readings to see if all the permissions were set correctly
(Side note; I knew it wasn't my VM because I created a larger instance machine before starting the process)
Next checked to see if my document root was correct and if I was in the correct absolute path 
Using the grep -R "DocumentRoot" /etc/apache2/sites-enabled/ command and it showed me the correct path
I also inspected the apache2 error logs using command sudo tail -n 20 /var/log/apache2/error.log
Looking for a 'file not found' error which wasn't there, meaning I now know 100% my file exsists 
Using sudo nano, I opened the apache config file to make sure those permissions were correct, sudo nano /etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf
I had to make sure since we were using .htaccess that ALLOWOVERIDE was set to All
Then hit the sudo systemctl restart apache2 command to make sure everything was pushed through
I was still getting 404 Error Not Found
I cleared my cache and changed my browser from ChromeOS to FireFox, as Dr. R suggested in office hours 
That still didn't work
Hindsight looking back to my (Side Note) when I created a new VM instance, that means an new IP address is assigned. 
I was using the older IP address from my BareBones OPAC not my new one 
Once that was changed and the new URL was typed the congratlations and startup page for WordPress showed up

Solutions
Make sure you IP address is correct, seems simple but super important
If that doesn't work, make sure your file exsist and is in the correct path
Always use sudo systemctl restart apache2 after each change you do to it, like changing permissions
Make sure your root document is correct
use ls -l if lost 
Most of the time apache2 is running and connected, make sure you are telling it exactly where to find your file
